  <main class="wrap article-body" id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <a class="back" href="../index.html">&larr; Back</a>
    <h1>Defense News Classifier</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">An LLM classifier for defense news, and the eval that graded every change.</p>

    <div class="decision" aria-label="Case study summary">
      <p class="tag">Case study summary</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Problem:</strong> Classify public defense news across category, operational domain, and region. A convincing demo is not proof of quality.</li>
        <li><strong>Ownership:</strong> I built the <Term id="classification">classifier</Term> and the eval harness. I labeled the <Term id="gold-set">gold set</Term>, defined the merge gate, and made the ship-or-cut decisions.</li>
        <li><strong>Constraints:</strong> The initial 300-row synthetic set graded model-written examples. The replacement human-labeled set had only 54 rows. Small apparent gains could therefore be noise.</li>
        <li><strong>Actions:</strong> I replaced the synthetic eval with real text and I tested a classical <Term id="baseline">baseline</Term>. I scaled a corroborating run to 300 examples. I measured retrieval, premium routing, and multi-agent review against held-out evidence.</li>
        <li><strong>Result and evidence:</strong> The shipped single-call classifier scores 94.4% category, 98.1% domain, and 94.4% region accuracy on the current gold. The gate declined three more complex approaches, and the simpler path stayed.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="lead">
      The classifier labels public defense-news text on three axes. The axes are
      category (procurement, operations, policy, technology, industry),
      operational domain (air, land, sea, cyber, space, multi), and region
      (indo-pacific, europe, middle-east, africa, americas, global). One model
      call applies
      all three labels. This page is the <Term id="eval">eval</Term>. It reports
      what the gold set did to the numbers, and which upgrades failed it.
    </p>

    <!-- Argument: the number fell when the gold got real, and that drop is
         the trustworthy reading. The state is a word plus a geometry first
         (FLATTERING against TRUSTWORTHY, ink against oxide). The numbers come
         second. This is not a colour-only chart, and it is not a second
         metrics table. ADR-010 does not apply. -->
    <div class="fig fig--plate" data-place="spine">
      <span class="fig-label">Plate 01</span>
      <svg class="eval-plate" viewBox="0 0 260 132" role="img"
           aria-label="The eval rebuild: v1 graded the model on 300 self-generated snippets and reported 97.3 percent domain accuracy. v2 replaced that with 54 hand-labeled real snippets and domain fell to 88.9 percent. The lower number is the trustworthy one.">
        <title>The eval rebuild: v1 self-graded 97.3 percent domain; v2 hand-labeled 88.9 percent. The drop is the trustworthy reading.</title>
        <defs>
          <marker id="ep-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5"
                  markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" />
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <text class="ep-lane" x="4" y="12">V1 SYNTHETIC</text>
        <rect class="ep-box" x="4" y="18" width="110" height="48" rx="2" />
        <text class="ep-figure" x="59" y="40" text-anchor="middle">97.3%</text>
        <text class="ep-micro" x="59" y="56" text-anchor="middle">domain, self-graded</text>

        <path class="ep-edge" d="M 116 42 L 140 42" marker-end="url(#ep-arrow)" aria-hidden="true" />

        <text class="ep-lane" x="146" y="12">V2 REAL</text>
        <rect class="ep-box" x="146" y="18" width="110" height="48" rx="2" />
        <text class="ep-figure" x="201" y="40" text-anchor="middle">88.9%</text>
        <text class="ep-micro" x="201" y="56" text-anchor="middle">domain, 54 gold</text>

        <text class="ep-lane" x="4" y="88">READING</text>
        <rect class="ep-ok" x="4" y="94" width="110" height="28" rx="2" />
        <text class="ep-ok-text" x="59" y="112" text-anchor="middle">FLATTERING</text>
        <rect class="ep-drop" x="146" y="94" width="110" height="28" rx="2" />
        <text class="ep-drop-text" x="201" y="112" text-anchor="middle">TRUSTWORTHY</text>
      </svg>
      <p class="eval-plate-caption">
        The number fell when the gold got real. Same model, harder test.
      </p>
    </div>

