    </p>

    <div class="toc-return"><a href="#toc-heading">Contents</a></div>
    <h2 id="stack">Stack</h2>
    <p>
      The stack is Python and the Anthropic SDK, with Sonnet 5 for
      classification and Opus as the judge that grades. pandas builds the eval
      tables, FastAPI serves the HTTP endpoint, and rank-bm25 ran the retired
      grounding experiment. scikit-learn appears in the eval dependencies only,
      for the classical baseline the model was measured against. Nothing in the
      shipped path uses it. pytest tests the code on mocked calls. The repo is
      public: <a href="https://github.com/sanlee-ys/defense-news-classifier">github.com/sanlee-ys/defense-news-classifier</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The eval harness, the gold set, and the ADRs are checkable. That includes
      the experiments I measured and cut.
    </p>

